#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068511 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "312677d3-ca04-520e-ae60-1725b65eefdb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving When the Right-Hand Side Is Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "580ca72e-31ba-591c-a5c4-08234ac9d2e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14827" :question/problem "Solve for $n$ where $n^2 +12n = 0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn^{2} + 12n &= 0 \\\\\nn(n + 12) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the zero product rule to get\n\n$$\nn=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad n+12=0\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nn=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad n=-12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $n=-12,0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068512 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51760e81-8cb9-557f-b010-196be8e5e1b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving When the Right-Hand Side Is Not Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "8e7b0730-4273-5eef-a9a3-4a9e91c62ff4" :question/math-academy-id "e-14829" :question/problem "Solve $3p^2 = 5p$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3p^2 &= 5p \\\\[3pt] 3p^2 - 5p &= 0 \\\\[3pt] p(3p - 5) &= 0 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by the zero product rule, we have\n\n$$\np=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad 3p-5=0\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\np=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad p=\\dfrac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\np=0,\\dfrac{5}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068513 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de81b6a4-0c3c-5f2f-b844-2cef931bec29" :knowledge-point/title "Solving When Both Sides are Quadratic"}] :question/id #uuid "4003ea24-f1cf-5abb-a3cb-033f8a11a6cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14831" :question/problem "Solve the equation $6x^2 +2x -2= 8x^2- x -2$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move all of the terms to the left-hand side and then factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6x^{2} + 2x - 2 &= 8x^{2} - x - 2 \\\\\n6x^{2} + 2x - 2 - (8x^{2} - x - 2) &= 0 \\\\\n6x^{2} + 2x - 2 - 8x^{2} + x + 2 &= 0 \\\\\n(6x^{2} - 8x^{2}) + (2x + x) + (-2 + 2) &= 0 \\\\\n- 2x^{2} + 3x + 0 &= 0 \\\\\n- 2x^{2} + 3x &= 0 \\\\\nx(-2x + 3) &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by the zero product rule, we have\n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad -2x + 3=0\n$$\n\nwhich in turn gives\n\n$$\nx=0 \\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad x=\\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51760e81-8cb9-557f-b010-196be8e5e1b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving When the Right-Hand Side Is Not Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "14879c25-f50a-5f08-9d0f-fcc77a6f475b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066207} {:answer-field/id #uuid "78500993-2a4f-5641-8cd7-0bc54ca0158b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066208}] :question/id #uuid "18ebe432-ec65-5059-b100-0754b81eac7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-223741" :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the solutions to $\\frac{2}{5}z^{2} =-2z$ are $z =$ {{field-1}} and $z =$\n{{field-2}}."}]}
